---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'April 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy — The Sustainability Diet" description="Privacy policy for sustainabilitydiet.com: what is collected, what is not, and why.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-reading px-6 pt-20 pb-32">

    <p class="small-caps text-xs text-ochre mb-4">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight leading-tight mb-4">
      Privacy.
    </h1>
    <p class="small-caps text-xs text-ink/50 mb-12">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose-reading text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/85 space-y-7">

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mt-8 mb-6">
        What this site collects.
      </h2>
      <p>
        The contact forms on this site are mail-client redirections.
        When you fill in one of the forms, your mail application
        opens with the form fields pre-filled, and you send the
        message from your own mail account. The site operator does
        not receive any data from the form except what you choose
        to send as an email. There is no form backend, no database,
        no analytics cookie dropped at submit, no third-party
        capture.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site uses <strong>no cookies</strong> at present, sets
        no local storage, and loads no third-party tracking scripts.
        Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts while the site is in
        build iteration; this loads stylesheets and font files from
        Google's CDN and, as part of that, Google's servers receive
        the HTTP request. Google Fonts' own documentation states
        that it logs request headers; the site operator does not
        see that data. Fonts will be self-hosted before the site
        reaches a permanent domain, at which point Google Fonts
        will not be loaded at all.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mt-12 mb-6">
        What happens to email you send.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Email you send to <a href="mailto:karen@paleofoundation.com" class="text-ochre hover:underline">karen@paleofoundation.com</a>
        is received and read by Karen Pendergrass. Content is used
        only to respond to your inquiry. Inquiries are not shared
        with third parties. Reader-updates inquiries are added to
        a short list used only to announce the book's publication
        and, later, major experiment milestones; this list is not
        shared or sold. Anyone on the reader-updates list can ask
        to be removed at any time by replying to any message with
        "remove."
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mt-12 mb-6">
        Hosting and server logs.
      </h2>
      <p>
        When this site moves to its hosting provider (planned:
        Vercel), the host will log standard request metadata
        (IP address, user agent, requested URL, timestamp) for a
        limited period for security and abuse-prevention purposes.
        This is hosting-provider-standard and not a feature of the
        site itself. No logs are read or analyzed by the site
        operator.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mt-12 mb-6">
        When this policy changes.
      </h2>
      <p>
        This page will note the last-updated date at the top of the
        page. Material changes &mdash; adding analytics, moving to
        an email-service provider with its own data processing, or
        adding any third-party capture &mdash; will be noted in the
        change log below.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mt-12 mb-6">
        Change log.
      </h2>
      <ul class="font-serif text-ink/75 space-y-2 pl-6 list-disc">
        <li>{lastUpdated} &mdash; initial policy.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mt-12 mb-6">
        Contact.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy, or requests to remove anything
        you have sent, go to <a href="mailto:karen@paleofoundation.com" class="text-ochre hover:underline">karen@paleofoundation.com</a>.
      </p>

    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
